{{Quote|I am A'Koba! I have slain a krayt dragon. I am a Tusken!|A'Koba|<ref name="Rites" />|translated=1}}
'''A'Koba''',<ref name="Rites" /> also known as '''URoRRuR'R'R''', was a skilled<ref name="Force Collection" /> but young [[Tusken Raider]] who lived on [[Tatooine]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]] and had cousins, [[A'Vor]] and [[A'Vor's twin]]. Shortly before the [[Battle of Yavin]], A'Koba attacked [[Luke Skywalker]] before getting scared off by [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]].<ref name="Rites" />

==Biography==
A'Koba<ref name="Rites" /> lived on the [[Outer Rim Territories|Outer Rim]] [[Planet|world]] of [[Tatooine]] during the [[Galactic Civil War]]<ref name="Episode IV" /> as part of [[Chief]]tain [[A'Yark]]'s [[A'Yark's tribe|tribe]].<ref name="Rites" /> Shortly before the [[Battle of Yavin]],<ref name="Episode IV" /> A'Koba, joined by his cousins, [[A'Vor]] and [[A'Vor's twin]], [[Death|killed]] a juvenile [[krayt dragon]] as a rite of passage into adulthood. He then claimed to A'Yark that he would be able to kill the adult krayts as well.<ref name="Rites" />

After being told of a mysterious [[shaman]] by A'Yark, A'Koba, having wanted to lead a hunt,<ref name="Rites" /> attacked [[Luke Skywalker]], a local [[moisture farmer]] who, along with [[protocol droid]] [[C-3PO]], was searching for his missing [[astromech droid]] [[R2-D2]]. A'Koba knocked Skywalker unconscious, and the Tusken<ref name="Episode IV" /> and his cousins<ref name="Rites" /> began searching Skywalker's [[landspeeder]]. They were scared off by [[Jedi Master]] [[Obi-Wan Kenobi]], who mimicked the call of a krayt dragon to spook A'Koba and his fellow Tusken Raiders into fleeing.<ref name="Episode IV" /> Upon seeing Kenobi, A'Koba realized he was the shaman A'Yark had warned them about.<ref name="Rites" />

==Behind the scenes==
A'Koba was played by stunt coordinator [[Peter Diamond]], who was the only stunt person on location in [[Tunisia]], in the [[1977]] film [[Star Wars: Episode IV A New Hope|''Star Wars'': Episode IV ''A New Hope'']].<ref name="Episode IV" /> Diamond actually only held aloft his [[gaderffii stick]] once. Editors [[Paul Hirsch]] and [[Richard Chew]] repeated and rewound such shot several times to make it seem Diamond had rocked it back and forth in triumph. A'Koba's famous bellow was added by sound designer [[Ben Burtt]], fashioned from [[Wikipedia:Donkey|donkey]] brays.<ref name="EoD">''[[Empire of Dreams: The Story of the Star Wars Trilogy]]''</ref> In [[Star Wars Legends|''Star Wars'' Legends]], the character was identified as [[URoRRuR'R'R]].<ref name="SWCG-ANHL:U">{{CCG|set=A New Hope Limited|cardname=URoRRuR'R'R}}</ref>

A'Koba's role in ''A New Hope'' closely resembles the one a [[Unidentified Knight of the Sith|member]] of the [[Knights of Sith]] had in the [[The Star Wars rough draft|rough draft]] of Episode IV.<ref name="TMoSW:TDSBtF">''[[The Making of Star Wars: The Definitive Story Behind the Original Film]]''</ref> The Knight ambushed [[Kane Starkiller]] along with his sons [[Annikin Starkiller|Annikin]] and [[Deak Starkiller|Deak]] at the [[Fourth Moon of Utapau]], killing the latter before getting killed by the former.<ref name="TSW:RD">[[The Star Wars rough draft|''The Star Wars'' rough draft]]</ref>

